Round gen_r4 done. I improved `impl/gen_pfa_small.c`, appended the r4 section to `strategies/gen_pfa_small.md`, and validated every gate on the final binary (single-call, two-step m=2, full graded chains, B=1, mixed remainder, generic sizes, bit-repeatability).

What the round established: gen_batchlane r3's register-explicit pencils are a **wash at 10/12 and a +12.6% regression at 15** on this engine (15 reverted to the memory form — the technique's win requires 2L + module temps ≤ ~32 registers); vdivpd re-beat the rcp14 ladder a third time (+1.9% at 12, paired); the one tuned-size win was moving the chain's m-loop inside the SCHED step function (−1.3% at L=20, bit-identical output); and the generic engine gained IPOK in-place pencils wherever Q ≡ 1 mod P (14/18/21/36/56, −1.9% at 36) for round-6 insurance.

**One-line report:** Two-sweep PFA SoA-8 with register-explicit 10/12 pencils, memory-form 15/20, fused vdivpd map, m-loop-in-SCHED chain, IPOK generic engine — batched chain best 1.155 / 1.966 / 4.444 / 13.123 us per transform at L=10/12/15/20, B=1 chain 3.869 / 5.258 / 14.140 / 31.966 us, single-call rel L2 2.6–3.1e-16 (two-step 0.8–1.2e-15 vs 3e-14 tol).
